# UI scripts

- **Prefab-based UI** (see `UI-SPEC.md` "Implementation conventions"): panel shells pre-placed in the scene; thin orchestrator controllers hold `[SerializeField]` refs (inspector-dragged). No `new GameObject` stacks or `RectTransform` math. **Fixed-slot UI** (Draft, Codex, build bar): pre-place N instances; runtime `Bind` only — no `Instantiate`. **Variable lists:** **bindable prefab view hierarchy** — pool authored child-view prefabs under serialized `Transform` parent(s); each tier exposes `Bind(domainData)`. Reference: `RunSummaryController` → `RunSummarySection` → `RunSummaryElement`. **Gameplay spawnables** (enemies, projectiles, gems, VFX) may instantiate/pool freely.
- **Bindable prefab view hierarchy:** orchestrator decides count/visibility; section/leaf prefabs own their widgets; grow pool with `Instantiate(prefab, parent)`, deactivate extras — never `Destroy` per refresh. Split monolithic controllers when they own repeating rows or nested `Apply*` helpers for each tier.
- **Same-prefab refs are inspector-dragged.** Do not `AddComponent`, `GetComponent`, `GetComponentInChildren`, or `TryGetComponent` in `Awake`/`Start` for components that live on the same prefab (self or children). Serialize `[SerializeField]` fields and assign them in the prefab. Missing refs → `Debug.LogError`, do not create or hunt at runtime. Allowed: EventSystem callbacks (`onClick` / interface handlers), `GetComponentInParent<Canvas>()` when the canvas is a scene ancestor, and `AddComponent`/`GetComponent` on objects you just spawned (drag ghost, pooled enemies, VFX). Do not use `EventTrigger` as a runtime event bus — implement the EventSystem interfaces on a dedicated handler component placed on the prefab.
- **TextMeshPro only** — `[SerializeField] TMP_Text` (or `TextMeshProUGUI`), `using TMPro;`. Never legacy `UnityEngine.UI.Text`. `Unity.TextMeshPro` asmdef ref required on UI assemblies.
- **No new bootstrap/wire-menu code** — existing `Phase2Pr*WireScene` menus are frozen (deleted pre-release); wiring is inspector-drag only.
- UGUI + feature.2d (UI sprites). Kenney-compatible — no shipping emoji.
- Follow `UI-SPEC.md` layout (docs repo).
- Conventional TD shell (place ghost, Shift multi-place, Esc/RMB cancel) follows Bloons TD 5/6 — see `gem-td-bloons-mechanics.mdc`.
- Selected-tower panel is **Tower Details** — never call it “inspector” (Unity Editor term).
- Socket DnD via drag handlers; listen to game events — do not poll domain state every frame.
- Canvas reference resolution 1920×1080.
